      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "We begin by evaluating each square root inside the ceiling function.\n\\[\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{9}}{\\sqrt{4}}=\\frac{3}{2}.\\]\nThe next step is to consider the ceiling of this value, which is the smallest integer greater than or equal to $\\frac{3}{2}.$\n\\[\\left\\lceil\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}}\\right\\rceil=2.\\]\nAt this point, we must evaluate the third square root inside the ceiling function.\n\\[\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2=\\frac{81}{16}.\\]\nThe next step is to consider the ceiling of this value, which is the smallest integer greater than or equal to $\\frac{81}{16}$.\n\\[\\left\\lceil\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2\\right\\rceil=5.\\]\nFinally, we can evaluate the original expression.\n\\[\\left\\lceil\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}}\\right\\rceil+\\left\\lceil\\frac{9}{4}\\right\\rceil+\\left\\lceil\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2\\right\\rceil=2+2+5=\\boxed{9}.\\]\nThe answer is: 9",
